{
  "name": "diff_impact",
  "description": "CALL THIS after every code change, BEFORE commit or push — never skip. USE WHEN: you have uncommitted changes and want to verify blast radius. NOT FOR: pre-edit analysis (use edit_context). vs edit_context: edit_context=pre-edit; diff_impact=post-edit. Omit all three for the unstaged working-tree diff, or provide at most one of: diff, staged=true, commits=<range>.",
  "inputSchema": {
    "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
    "properties": {
      "diff": {
        "description": "A raw unified diff (`git diff` output) to analyze directly, instead\nof having this tool run git itself. At most one of `diff`, `staged`,\n`commits` may be set — omitting all three analyzes the unstaged\nworking-tree diff (plain `git diff`).",
        "type": [
          "string",
          "null"
        ]
      },
      "staged": {
        "description": "`true` to analyze the staged diff (`git diff --cached`); `false` or\nomitted analyzes the unstaged working-tree diff. At most one of\n`diff`, `staged`, `commits` may be set.",
        "type": [
          "boolean",
          "null"
        ]
      },
      "commits": {
        "description": "A commit range/rev understood by `git diff`, e.g. `HEAD~3..HEAD` or\na single commit SHA. At most one of `diff`, `staged`, `commits`\nmay be set.",
        "type": [
          "string",
          "null"
        ]
      }
    },
    "type": "object"
  },
  "outputSchema": {
    "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
    "$defs": {
      "ErrorDetail": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "code": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "message": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "recoverable": {
            "type": "boolean"
          },
          "review": {
            "description": "Set only on HIGH_RISK_REQUIRES_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW / DIFF_DIGEST_MISMATCH — everything needed to relay-approve/decline via review_decide_via_agent_relay.",
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "$ref": "#/$defs/PendingReviewPacket"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ]
          },
          "next_call": {
            "description": "The exact next tool call this error implies, if unambiguous — same shape as suggested_next.",
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "$ref": "#/$defs/SuggestedNext"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "code",
          "message",
          "recoverable"
        ]
      },
      "PendingReviewPacket": {
        "description": "Wave 3 (audit follow-up, 2026-08-23): the structured shape of a\n`HIGH_RISK_REQUIRES_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW`/`DIFF_DIGEST_MISMATCH` error's\n`review` field -- lets a calling agent relay-approve/decline without\never reading `pending_reviews` directly or reimplementing\n`hash_content` itself.\n\nWave 14 (audit follow-up, 2026-08-24): `diff_digest` is NOT\n`hash_content` of THIS packet's own `diff_preview` field -- it's\n`hash_content` of the full, unsanitized, uncapped diff stored server-\nside (see `from_pending`'s own comment). It exists to prove identity/\nfreshness (\"this is really the review you fetched, not a stale or\nguessed copy\"), not to let a caller verify \"the text I'm looking at\nhashes to this\" -- that's structurally impossible to guarantee anyway,\nsince different surfaces (this JSON packet vs. `calm review show`'s\nterminal output) apply different sanitize/cap transforms to the same\nunderlying diff and can't all match one digest. Callers must always\nCOPY this value verbatim, never recompute it from `diff_preview`.",
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "review_id": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "diff_preview": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "preview_truncated": {
            "description": "`true` when `diff_preview` was cut down from the full diff\n`diff_digest` covers -- see the struct's own doc comment.",
            "type": "boolean"
          },
          "diff_digest": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "expires_at": {
            "type": "number",
            "format": "double"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "review_id",
          "diff_preview",
          "preview_truncated",
          "diff_digest",
          "expires_at"
        ]
      },
      "SuggestedNext": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "tool": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "reason": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "args": true,
          "gate": {
            "description": "true iff skipping `tool` is hook-enforced, not just advisory.",
            "type": [
              "boolean",
              "null"
            ]
          },
          "required_user_input": {
            "description": "Names any `tool` param intentionally left out of `args` because only a human can safely supply it (e.g. `approve`). Absent means `args` is already complete.",
            "type": [
              "array",
              "null"
            ],
            "items": {
              "type": "string"
            }
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "tool",
          "reason"
        ]
      },
      "AffectedSymbolOutput": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "qualified_name": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "name": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "path": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "kind": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "signature_changed": {
            "type": "boolean"
          },
          "symbol_is_new": {
            "description": "True when this symbol didn't exist before the diff (new file, or a\npure-addition hunk covering its signature) — it has zero prior call\nsites by definition, so `signature_changed` is always false for it\nand risk is not escalated on \"callers may need update\" grounds.",
            "type": "boolean"
          },
          "blast_radius": {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/BlastRadiusOutput"
          },
          "risk_assessment": {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/RiskAssessmentOutput"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "qualified_name",
          "name",
          "path",
          "kind",
          "signature_changed",
          "symbol_is_new",
          "blast_radius",
          "risk_assessment"
        ]
      },
      "BlastRadiusOutput": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "direct_callers": {
            "type": "integer",
            "format": "int64"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "direct_callers"
        ]
      },
      "RiskAssessmentOutput": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "level": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "reasons": {
            "type": "array",
            "items": {
              "type": "string"
            }
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "level",
          "reasons"
        ]
      },
      "UnindexedFileOutput": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "path": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "reason": {
            "description": "\"pending_scan\" — a recognized source file, in a path the indexer\nactually walks, that just hasn't been scanned yet; resolves itself\nonce indexing catches up (check `indexing_status`).\n\"out_of_scope\" — will stay unindexed no matter how long you wait:\neither not a source extension the indexer parses at all (docs,\nconfig, etc.), or it sits under a dotdir/`IGNORE_DIRS` path (e.g.\n`.claude/`, `target/`) the walker categorically never descends into,\nregardless of extension.\n\"recognized_unparsed\" — a `file_index` row exists (the indexer has\nscanned it) but `language` is NULL: a recognized-but-unsupported\nextension (see `is_recognized_unparsed_extension`) tracked by path\nonly. Like \"out_of_scope\", this never resolves on its own — there is\nno symbol extraction to wait for — but unlike \"out_of_scope\" the file\ngenuinely is indexed (has a row), just never for symbols.\n\"deleted\" — the file appears in the diff but no longer exists on\ndisk (deleted or renamed away); like \"out_of_scope\" this is a\npermanent state — it will never be scanned no matter how long you\nwait — so it must never gate `aggregate_risk` on `indexing_status`.",
            "type": "string"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "path",
          "reason"
        ]
      }
    },
    "required": [
      "flow_state"
    ],
    "type": "object",
    "properties": {
      "flow_state": {
        "description": "Wave 11 (item 3, \"unified continuation state machine\"): present on\nevery response regardless of success/error -- `\"ready\"` on success,\nor one of `needs_context`/`needs_human_review`/`needs_verification`/\n`blocked` on error (see `classify_error_state`'s own doc comment).\nLets an agent dispatch on ONE top-level field instead of\nmaintaining its own per-`code` remediation table across ~70\ndistinct codes.\n\nNamed `flow_state`, not the more obvious `state` (audit follow-up,\n2026-08-23): several tool-specific success structs (e.g.\n`EditTransactionStatusOutput`, `VerifyChangeOutput` in txn.rs) have\ntheir own unrelated `state` field, and this struct's `success: T` is\n`#[serde(flatten)]`ed -- a same-named field there would silently\nserialize as a SECOND `\"state\"` JSON key (serde's flatten writes\neach field independently; nothing dedupes it), with most JSON\nparsers then last-write-wins-ing over whichever value serialized\nsecond. `flow_state` is deliberately namespaced so no domain output\nstruct will ever pick the same name by coincidence again.",
        "type": "string"
      },
      "error": {
        "anyOf": [
          {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/ErrorDetail"
          },
          {
            "type": "null"
          }
        ]
      },
      "files_changed": {
        "type": "array",
        "items": {
          "type": "string"
        }
      },
      "affected_symbols": {
        "type": "array",
        "items": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/AffectedSymbolOutput"
        }
      },
      "unindexed_files": {
        "type": "array",
        "items": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/UnindexedFileOutput"
        }
      },
      "aggregate_risk": {
        "type": "string"
      },
      "suggested_reviewers": {
        "type": "array",
        "items": {
          "type": "string"
        }
      },
      "note": {
        "type": [
          "string",
          "null"
        ]
      },
      "suggested_next": {
        "anyOf": [
          {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/SuggestedNext"
          },
          {
            "type": "null"
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  },
  "annotations": {
    "readOnlyHint": true,
    "destructiveHint": false,
    "idempotentHint": true,
    "openWorldHint": false
  }
}
